Subject: [PATCH 08019/11362] [outer-loop] The induced world models fail in two
 OPPOSITE ways -- no-op (12/33) and runaway writer (21/33)

The bottleneck note ended by asking what error class the induced engines fall into and
calling it a cheap CPU-only follow-up. It was cheap enough to do immediately: the counts
were already recorded per row in exp6012 (`correct_changed_cells`,
`spurious_changed_cells`, `noop_hallucination_rate`). The 33 rows split cleanly, and the
split matters because the two modes want OPPOSITE corrections.

MODE A -- the no-op world model (12/33: ar25, ka59, re86, and cd82 on changed frames).
correct_changed_cells = 0 AND spurious_changed_cells = 0. The engine predicts that nothing
ever changes. It is the identity engine in all but name, which is precisely why it scores
respectably on exact-match accuracy -- most cells genuinely do not change -- while scoring
zero on changed-cell recall. This is the mechanism behind the intermediate exact-accuracy
values (0.125-0.6) that sat next to ~0.003 cell recall.

MODE B -- the runaway writer (21/33: cn04, dc22, g50t, m0r0, sc25, sk48, wa30). It does
write, but writes 3x-10x MORE changed cells than reality contains: cn04@1 has 4346 true
changed cells against 33021 spurious ones, g50t@0 1504 against 14612, sc25@0 453 against
4687. And noop_hallucination_rate reaches 1.0 on cn04@0 -- on frames where reality did
nothing, the engine invents a change every single time.

WHY THE SPLIT IS THE POINT. Mode A needs the inducer to predict any dynamics at all; Mode B
needs it CONSTRAINED from over-writing. A single undifferentiated "make the inducer better"
intervention is unlikely to move both, which is a plausible reading of why the 27B -> 31B
migration (a ~6x better generator) banked zero additional levels. Mode B in particular is
directly addressable by a change-magnitude prior or a sparsity constraint on predicted
writes, and that is cheap to test; Mode A looks like a failure to extract action semantics.

cd82 is a mixture -- no-op on changed frames, but hallucinating at 0.44-0.55 on no-op
frames -- and is flagged as such rather than forced into one bucket.

